<p>
  The headline result: with <strong>87.1% fewer attention interactions</strong> per layer,
  VECA reaches within 0.28 mIoU of its DINOv3 teacher on dense segmentation,
  and within 1.87% on ImageNet classification. This strongly suggests that direct
  patch-to-patch attention — the defining operation of the ViT — is not strictly
  necessary for high-quality visual representations.
</p>

<div class="callout">
  <b>Implications for scaling:</b> Linear-time attention means VECA can process 4K images with the
  same FLOPs as a standard ViT processes 1K images. As image resolution keeps growing (medical imaging,
  satellite imagery, robotics), this O(N) complexity may become decisive. Combined with elastic inference,
  VECA suggests a future where the compute budget is a <em>dial</em>, not a design choice.
</div>

<!-- Listen-friendly summary (hidden, for audio playback) -->
<div class="listen-friendly-content" style="display:none;" aria-hidden="true">
  <div lang="en">
    <h2>Audio Summary: VECA — Vision Transformers Without Patch-to-Patch Attention</h2>
    <p>VECA, or Visual Elastic Core Attention, is a new Vision Transformer architecture that eliminates the quadratic cost of standard self-attention by routing all patch communication through a small set of learned core tokens. Standard ViTs require N-squared pairwise interactions between patches; VECA replaces this with only 2NC plus C-squared interactions, where C is the number of core tokens. At 512-pixel resolution with 64 cores, this means 87 percent fewer attention operations per layer.</p>
    <p>The core tokens are resolution-invariant and learned from scratch. Patches attend only to cores; cores attend to all patches and to each other. Information still flows across the full image, but with graph diameter two instead of one. A key feature is elastic inference: by varying C from 8 to 64 at test time using nested dropout training, the model trades accuracy for speed without retraining. On ImageNet-1K classification, VECA with 64 cores achieves 81.93 percent versus DINOv3's 83.56 percent. On PASCAL Context segmentation, it achieves 57.46 mIoU versus 57.74 for its teacher, a gap of just 0.28 despite 87 percent fewer attention interactions. Notably, core tokens develop emergent semantic organization across layers without explicit supervision, transitioning from isotropic representations to semantically clustered object-centric structures.</p>
  </div>
  <div lang="zh">
    <h2>语音摘要：VECA——无需像素对像素注意力的视觉Transformer</h2>
    <p>VECA（视觉弹性核心注意力）是一种新型视觉Transformer架构，通过将所有图像块的通信路由到一组小型学习核心令牌，消除了标准自注意力的二次方计算代价。标准ViT需要N²次图像块间的两两交互；VECA用仅2NC加C²次交互取而代之，其中C为核心令牌数量。在512像素分辨率、64个核心令牌的情况下，每层注意力计算量减少87%。</p>
    <p>核心令牌与分辨率无关，从头开始学习。图像块只关注核心令牌，核心令牌则关注所有图像块和彼此。信息仍然在整幅图像中流通，但图距从1变为2。关键特性是弹性推理：通过在训练时使用嵌套dropout，测试时可在不重新训练的情况下将C从8调整到64，从而在精度和速度之间权衡。在ImageNet-1K分类任务上，64核VECA达到81.93%，而DINOv3为83.56%。在PASCAL Context语义分割上，VECA达到57.46 mIoU，其教师模型为57.74，差距仅0.28，但注意力计算量减少了87%。值得注意的是，核心令牌在无需显式监督的情况下，在各层间展现出从各向同性表示到语义聚类的目标中心结构的涌现性组织能力。</p>
  </div>
</div>
